<h1>Dospherequalification()</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="description"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Launches sphere alignment wizard, used to align the sensor to the arm coordinate system</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Format</font></span></b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">:</font></span></p>
<p class="Code"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">DoSphereQualification</font></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">(</font></span><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Radius, WarningLevelStandardDeviation, ErrorLevelStandardDeviation, WarningLevelConditionNumber, ErrorLevelConditionNumber, AcceptAboveWarningLevel,&#160; QualificationFileName)</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Parameters</font></span></b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">:</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><i style="font-style:italic;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Radius</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">- radius of the certified sphere. If omitted in the full parameter description its last value is used. If omitted and no last value, a default 15.0061mm value is used.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><i style="font-style:italic;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>WarningLevelStandardDeviation</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">– defines the std dev value, above which the sphere qualification may be accepted or rejected depending on the user's decision.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><i style="font-style:italic;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>ErrorLevelStandardDeviation</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">- – defines the std dev value, above which the sphere qualification will be rejected.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><i style="font-style:italic;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>WarningLevelConditionNumber</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">- defines the condition number value, above which the sphere qualification may be accepted or rejected depending on the user's decision.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><i><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>ErrorLevelConditionNumber</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">- defines the condition number value, above which the sphere qualification will be rejected.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="p2"><span lang="EN-GB"><b style="font-weight:bold;">N</b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">ote</font>: A very good alignment could be achieved at Standard deviation below 30 microns and Condition number closer to 20.</span></span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><i style="font-style:italic;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>AcceptAboveWarningLevel</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">-&#160; is Yes/No and when the procedure is started via COM client defines whether the sphere qualification will be accepted even if one of the values - StandardDeviation or ConditionNumber number is above warning level. Default value == no. This parameter is ignored in the manual SQ procedure - message will always appear asking whether to accept or reject the SQ.</span></p>
<p class="parameterdescription" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><i style="font-style:italic;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>QualificationFileName</b></span></i> <span lang="EN-GB">- In manual SQ mode if QualificationFileName is specified the function will save directly the new alignment under that name. If "" is passed (the default value) a log display window and a File Save dialog will appear. Via COM client a file name must be specified, otherwise an error will occur.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">Note</font></span></b><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><font size="2" style="font-size:10pt;">: The parameter names could be omitted. In this case their values should follow the order, specified above.</font></span></p>
<p class="parameterstitle" style="font-size:10.0pt; font-family:Arial;"><b style="font-weight:bold;"><span lang="EN-GB">UI Commands:</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:normal;">N</span>one</b></p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Example for manual procedure:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode"><span lang="EN-GB">DoSphereQualification( Radius=15.001, WarningLevelStandardDeviation=0.04,&#160; ErrorLevelStandardDeviation=0.06, WarningLevelConditionNumber=30,&#160; ErrorLevelConditionNumber=50,&#160; AcceptAboveWarningLevel=Yes,&#160; QualificationFileName=”MMD100_Sph_10.08.2007” )</span></p>
<p class="ExampleCode">&#160;</p>
<p class="ExampleCode">Example for procedure via COM client:</p>
<p class="ExampleCode"><span lang="EN-GB">DoSphereQualification( 15.001, 0.04, 0.06, 30, 50, Yes, ”MMD100_Sph_10.08.2007” )</span></p>
<p>&#160;</p>
